ations for  example if the phones on my desk the one  thing that I definitely really missed  was the super fast app switching by  sliding my fingers across the bottom bar  on the new phones the speakers are  better than I expected  getting really close to the much larger  iPhone 11 but just like the iPhone 8 and  10 the earpiece speaker is still quieter  than on the newer phone  so if you're watching videos it does  seem a little bit out of balance having  more sound coming from the bottom firing  speaker  [Music]  I definitely think that Apple could have  made a few small improvements like the  earpiece speaker but I also understand  why they didn't because they really  wanted to hit that 399 price point and  spend the extra money on other things  another thing that wasn't upgraded were  the cameras now everybody expected that  se to have the same exact cameras as the  iPhone 10 are and the 10s but that's  actually not true we first found this  out in our comparison where the selfie  camera could only record 1080p at 30  frames per second where the 10r could do  1080p 60 and the 11 could do 4k 60 this  was really odd and the only explanation  was that Apple kept the same  front-facing camera as in the iPhone 8 a  few days later iFixit published their  teardown and I was very surprised that  the rear camera is also from the 8th  meaning it is really old in terms of  text since the last two years brought  major upgrades with larger faster  sensors now what surprised me even more  than that was how good the photos looked  there was a huge difference in photo  quality going from the iPhone 8 to the  10r when we tested them but the old  sensors in the SE are now taking  noticeably better photos than the 10 are  in the 10s the dynamic range is better  details better and even noise is lower  this just shows how much software and  processing matters for photos and Apple  definitely knew that when they put the  same a 13 Bionic processor in this $400  phone that's in my $1100 iPhone 11 Pro  max because of it the SE has a new smart  HDR tech and in good lighting the images  look as good as the iPhone 11 Pro which  is crazy in lower lighting the 11 looks  better due to deep fusion tech which  isn't possible due to the slower sensor  and the same thing goes with night mode  which is a bummer with that said in  pretty much every case the SE beats out  the iPhone 10s and 10 R which logically  doesn't make sense because the hardware  is older but it does I went ahead and  set up a blind photo comparison that I'm  gonna have Vadim do so if you want to  see the SE stack up against these other  iPhones and if you want to see if a team  actually tell a difference make sure you  guys are subscribed then you have  notifications enabled after testing it  out my view of the SE is much better  than it was before and I think that most  people that have older iPhones are gonna  be extremely happy with it at $399 for a  64 gigabyte model I can see so many  people who are hanging on to dying  iPhones finally upgrading I can also see  a lot of people upgrading from budget  Android phones both old ones and new  ones in finally getting an iPhone  because of the really low price and that  in turn is gonna make Apple a lot of  money on services down the line now my  two biggest complaints were the lack of  the ultra wide lens and the telephoto  which I love and use all the time and  the battery life now I use my phone all  the time which is why I love the iPhone  11 Pro max which has a massive battery  but thankfully from the comparisons I've  seen online the new S II actually can  get about an hour extra screen on time  compared to the iPhone 8 thanks to that  new a 13 processor and of course the S  II does support fast charging they have  to buy afterwards Apple's costs a lot  but I have a link in the video  description to a charger that is  certified and comes with a cable for  only $17 altum Utley I am going back to  my iPhone 11 pro max but you can count  on me finally breaking my huge iPhone  trend that has been going on for many  years and next time around going for a  smaller iPhone all thanks to trying out  the new iPhone se thank you guys for  watching let me know your thoughts down  in the comment section below click that  little circle above if you guys want to  see our full review of the S key and if  you want to see the comparisons we have  somewhere right over there this has been  maxed and I'll see you in the next video  [Music]
 

